# Simple Money Playbook automation engine.
# Allow-list: track ONLY the daily-engine directories; ignore everything else under income/.
/*
!/.gitignore
# Line-ending normalization. Root files are ignored by default by the /* rule above, so this needs an
# explicit allow or a fresh clone silently loses it and the whole-file-diff problem comes straight back.
!/.gitattributes
!/README.md
!/grocery/
!/meal-prep/
# SHARED CODE THE BUILDERS CANNOT RUN WITHOUT. lib\ held ghost-lib.ps1 (dot-sourced by every publisher)
# and, from 2026-07-31, design-tokens.ps1 (dot-sourced by all three page builders) while being entirely
# untracked - a fresh clone of this repo could not build a single page. Same class as the "the agent
# prompts are code" finding below: the thing every script depends on was the thing nobody versioned.
# design\ carries the specs those builders implement, which is the only record of WHY the markup is
# shaped the way it is.
!/lib/
!/design/
# The join interstitial's SOURCE. deploy-interstitial.ps1 was tracked while the payload it deploys was
# not, so the only copy of a script running on every page of the site was one machine's disk plus a
# minified blob inside Ghost settings. Same class as lib\ above.

!/site/
# The GPU semantic sidecar: SOURCE is tracked, the environment is not. .venv is several GB of wheels and
# the model weights are another ~4.5 GB pulled from HuggingFace on first run; both are reproducible from
# requirements.txt and the pinned model ids in lib_match.py. data\ and out\ are derived from the feeds.
!/sidecar/
/sidecar/.venv/
# NOTE the trailing /* rather than /. Git does not descend into an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so a
# later negation for a path inside it can never match - the frozen snapshots below stayed
# invisible until this line was changed from `/sidecar/data/` to `/sidecar/data/*`.
/sidecar/data/*
# ...EXCEPT the frozen evaluation snapshots. data/ is a working directory and is rightly
# ignored, but a snapshot is an evaluation RECORD, and the argument is the one made for the
# gold set below: a record that does not outlive the machine that produced it is not a record.
# It exists because commodity_text() is label + TODAY's accepted exemplars, so every score in
# the estate drifts with the shelf - measured 2026-08-22, dropping the exemplars moves TASK A
# AUC from 0.9705 to 0.7921, and the same eval files scored 24/24 on 08-01 and 17/25 on 08-22
# with no model change at all. A stock-vs-candidate comparison must pin both sides to one
# snapshot (sidecar/freeze_eval.py) or it measures the board. ~850 KB each.
!/sidecar/data/frozen/
# ...and the LABELLED near-miss set, for the same reason one step further. mine-candidates.json is
# a 13-second bi-encoder pass and is rightly derived, but the LABELS come from commodities.json's
# regex, which drifts: re-labelling next month gives a different file, so a comparison against
# today's mined AUC would measure the rules rather than the model. It is the third evaluation
# record in this estate, beside the frozen defs and the gold set. ~950 KB.
!/sidecar/data/mine-labelled.json
# ...and the ADJUDICATED rulings on those pairs, which is the strongest case for tracking in this
# whole file: a reasoner looked at a product and a commodity and ruled. It cost tokens, it cannot be
# recomputed by any script, and authority.py gives it the same tier as the Claude review lane.
!/sidecar/data/mine-adjudicated.json
# The corpus MANIFEST but not the corpus. train/test.jsonl are 4 MB of text reproducible from the
# graph + the two records above; the manifest is the split - seed, holdout families, per-source
# counts - and without it "which rows did that model see" has no answer.
!/sidecar/data/pair-corpus*/
/sidecar/data/pair-corpus*/*.jsonl
# Candidate cross-encoders (finetune_reranker.py). 2.2 GB of weights each, reproducible from the
# corpus manifest + the training card inside the directory, and never the pinned model - a candidate
# is reached only through --reranker. The CARD is the record and is small enough to keep.
# (and note the /*/* - git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, the same trap this file
# already documents twenty lines up, and which it fell into again on 2026-08-23.)
/sidecar/models/*/*
!/sidecar/models/*/training-card.json
/sidecar/out/*
!/sidecar/out/backtest-report.md
!/sidecar/out/phase2-report.md
# The hard eval is the reason the identity lane is still off. Its numbers have to outlive the machine
# that produced them, or the only surviving evidence is Phase 1's AUC 0.985 - which was measured on
# negatives so dramatic (bath soap as coconut oil) that it answered a question nobody was asking.
!/sidecar/out/hardeval-report.md
!/sidecar/out/hardeval.json
# The TAGGED eval records too (backtest.py/hardeval.py --tag). These are baselines a fine-tune
# is measured against months later; an evaluation record that does not outlive the machine that
# produced it is not a record. Tens of KB each.
!/sidecar/out/backtest-*.json
!/sidecar/out/hardeval-*.json
!/sidecar/out/hardeval-report-*.md
# The rule gaps a reasoner found: pairs where a commodity's own include patterns reject a product
# that IS that commodity. Each one is a live board defect and none of them is applied by any script,
# so if this file is not tracked the finding exists only until the next run overwrites it.
!/sidecar/out/mined-rule-gaps.json
# The seed sweep that reverted a promotion: four trainings per arm, corpus and recipe fixed. It is
# the reason the gate now requires >= 3 seeds, and a rule whose evidence is not kept is a rule the
# next person will argue with.
!/sidecar/out/seed-sweep-*.json
# The audit of the local model's own rejections: 192 adjudicated rulings and the two rates they
# produce. It is the only measurement anyone has ever made of whether that model's 3,315 unreviewed
# rejections are correct, it cost a review session, and no script can recompute it.
!/sidecar/out/rejection-audit.json
/sidecar/**/__pycache__/
# The member-tool SOURCES and the build scripts that publish them. Same hole as lib\ and the interstitial:
# these run on the live site, several are the only copy in existence, and none of them were versioned
# while unrelated tool HTML at the same path was. Swept in 2026-08-01.
# the agent prompts + scheduled-task SKILLs that DRIVE the estate, plus the audit that proves the backup is
# current. They live under C:\Codex\.claude and C:\Users\Owner\.claude, neither of which is a repository, so
# without this they were the only unversioned code in the system (2026-07-31).
!/ops/
!/.github/
!/public/
!/worker/
# The knowledge graph (graph-native redesign, Phase 0-6). Same split as sidecar\
# above: SOURCE and DURABLE STATE are tracked, the derived index and the model
# environment are not. graph\sqlite\graph.db is an INDEX, rebuildable in seconds
# from the tracked nodes/edges/aliases/provenance JSON, and graph\.gitignore
# excludes it plus the per-run scratch under graph\runs\. The gold set and the
# provenance JSONL ARE tracked: they are the evaluation record and the audit
# trail, and a gold set that does not outlive the machine that produced it is
# not a gold set. Model weights (~13 GB) live OUTSIDE the repo at C:\Codex\llm
# and are refetched by tools\local-llm\fetch-model.ps1.
!/graph/
!/tools/
!/wrangler.jsonc
!/platform/
# THE 52-WEEK CURRICULUM AND ITS SUPPORTING DOCS (2026-08-08). lessons\ holds the local ORIGINAL of 55
# pages that are live right now - the sitemap serves every one of them as week-N-<slug>. They were ignored
# by the /* rule above and therefore existed on exactly one machine's disk, unversioned, while the tracked
# lesson content on the site depended on them. Same "only copy in existence" hole as lib\ and the
# interstitial. Worth naming how it hid: an earlier sweep for published-pages-without-a-local-source
# matched repo BASENAMES (lesson-04-the-gap-is-the-score) against Ghost SLUGS (week-4-the-gap-is-the-score)
# and scored zero, so 55 pages with a perfectly good local source were classified as Ghost-only. A
# basename-equality scan cannot answer that question when the publisher renames.
!/content/
# CURRICULUM.md is the plan those 55 lessons implement and 13 of them cite it by name; STYLE-GUIDE.md is
# the voice spec CURRICULUM.md and README.md both point at. Ignoring the spec while tracking nothing that
# explains it is how the WHY gets lost - the same reason design\ is tracked.
!/docs/
# The four downloadable workbooks. Each is READ (not generated) by a build-*.ps1 that is already tracked
# above, so a fresh clone had the publisher and not the payload - the exact shape of the lib\ hole.
# get-starthere.ps1 reads this for the /start-here/ Ghost post id. 49 bytes of durable state that cannot
# be recomputed from anything else in the repo.
# brand\ is the logo, cover art and social imagery - the visual identity, in one place, with no other copy.
!/brand/
# The pre-Ghost Substack archive: 71 posts, the published form of the same content lessons\ now carries
# (word-for-word overlap on the weeks that exist in both). Superseded, never regenerable, cheap to keep.

# --- top-level paths left OUT of the allow-list ON PURPOSE. Recorded because the /* rule makes "ignored"
#     and "nobody thought about it" look identical from the outside, which is how lessons\ and brand\ went
#     unversioned for two months. check-uncommitted-source.ps1 -Ignored enforces this list. ---
# facebook\ - both PNGs are byte-identical (SHA-256) to brand\FBCover.png and brand\FBProfile.png, which
#             are now tracked. A second copy of a tracked file is not a second source.
# out\      - interstitial-deploy.html, rebuilt by deploy-interstitial.ps1 from the tracked
#             join-interstitial.html. Derived output, same rule as grocery\out\.
# seo-backlink-plan.md - a one-off plan doc from 2026-07-10 that nothing in the repo references and no
#             build step reads. Notes, not source.

# --- regenerable pipeline OUTPUTS: recomputed every run from the raw inputs, so never tracked. This lets
#     the local browser agents commit their raw store data without derived-file rebase conflicts vs the
#     cloud, and keeps the repo to source-of-truth inputs + durable state only. ---
/grocery/out/comparison-*.json
/grocery/out/*candidates*.json
/grocery/out/records-*.json
/grocery/out/flagged-*.json
/grocery/out/guards-*.json
/grocery/out/verified-*.json
/grocery/out/verify-input-*.json
/grocery/out/recipe-board.json
/grocery/out/recipe-sales-*.json
/grocery/out/recipe-costs.json
/grocery/out/deals-page*.html
/grocery/out/link-audit.json
/grocery/out/name-drift.json
# the arrivals desk's daily docket: a pure function of the comparison-*.json boards (themselves ignored above)
# plus commodities.json, rewritten from scratch every run at 35-45 KB. push-data.ps1 ends in `git add -A`, so
# without this line every daily and weekly run would commit a churning derived file that nothing reads back -
# the same regenerable-output rule that already covers name-drift.json and link-audit.json directly above.
/grocery/out/arrivals-docket.json
/grocery/out/url-worklist.json
# the walled-store rescue worklists: build-rescue-worklist.ps1 rewrites all four from scratch on every ad
# cycle out of the comparison boards (ignored above) plus the capture files, and their whole job is to be
# TODAY's list - a tracked copy would churn daily through push-data's `git add -A` and, worse, invite
# someone to read a committed one as current. Same regenerable-output rule as url-worklist.json above.
/grocery/out/rescue-terms-*.txt
# input-fingerprint stamp for audit-match-soundness: a pure function of files already in the repo, rewritten
# whenever any of them changes, and 1.24 MB a time - regenerable output, never a source of truth
/grocery/out/audit/match-sweep-cache.json
# machine-local runtime lock: it is HELD while the weekly run is in flight, and -Phase links ends in
# push-data's `git add -A`, so tracking it would commit a live lock (pid + 4h expiry) to the shared repo and
# rebase-conflict with every other machine - the same reason triage-queue.json is ignored
/grocery/out/weekly-run.lock
/grocery/out/smp-feed.json
/grocery/out/recipe-board-everyday.bak-*.json
# rolling local archive of aged out\ snapshots (run-daily-local.ps1 retention moves files in and later
# deletes them; tracking it would make push-data's `git add -A` commit stale data and churn on every purge)
/grocery/out/archive/
# per-item sale-window log (sale price + start/end dates): derived from the board daily, self-heals, not tracked
/grocery/sale-windows.json
# local ops-alert triage queue + its drain state: machine-local by design (the cloud runner's copy would be
# ephemeral anyway, and tracking it would rebase-conflict every day). Cloud failures reach Brad via /ops-alert.
/grocery/triage-queue.json
# the graph's learning + escalation queues: same class as triage-queue.json above. Producer (the daily
# pipeline / resolver) and consumer (the learning loop, the Claude review agent) are on the SAME PC, so
# these never cross the git-bus, and their bodies carry raw store product text. Durable learning records
# live in the graph (learning_proposals / approved_patches) and in graph\provenance\, both of which ARE
# tracked - so nothing auditable is lost by ignoring the queues themselves.
/grocery/learning-queue.json
/grocery/escalation-queue.json
/grocery/escalation-review-packet.json
# Kroger-API evaluation captures: raw pulls kept for analysis, deliberately NOT board inputs (the
# "N ct / M oz" size ambiguity underprices some cells; see pull-regular-bakers-api.ps1 header)
/grocery/out/kroger-api-eval/
# heavy Baker's flyer captures (intermediate; parsed into bakers-deals-*.json, then not needed).
# pages.staging/ + ad-window.json are the 2026-08-09 install contract (adpages-lib.ps1): pages land in
# staging and swap in only when complete, and the stamp records which ad window the images belong to.
/grocery/out/bakers/*.jpg
/grocery/out/bakers/meta.json
/grocery/out/bakers/urls.txt
/grocery/out/bakers/pages.staging/
/grocery/out/bakers/ad-window.json

# heavy Fareway ad-page captures (intermediate; vision-read into fareway-deals-*.json, then not needed)
/grocery/out/fareway/weekly/
/grocery/out/fareway/monthly/
/grocery/out/fareway/weekly.staging/
/grocery/out/fareway/monthly.staging/

# ad-hoc item-onboarding vet outputs (isolated diff-board runs while adding a batch; throwaway diagnostics)
/grocery/out/after-*.json
/grocery/out/detA-*.json
/grocery/out/detB-*.json
/grocery/out/final-batch1-*.json
/grocery/out/staples500/*.bak

# --- never commit, anywhere in the tree ---
# secrets (the Ghost admin key lives here locally; it is a GitHub Actions secret in CI)
.ghostkey
# Kroger/Baker's developer API client id + secret (developer.kroger.com). Local only; if this ever runs
# in the cloud it goes in as GitHub Actions secrets, never in a tracked file.
.krogerkey
*.secret
*_secret*
ghost-config.ps1
# heavy / generated binaries
*.mp4
*.exe
*.zip
# noise
*.log
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
grocery/out/captures/
grocery/logs-archive/
!/archive/
/archive/site-backups/*
!/archive/site-backups/ghost-export-*.zip

# tool-generated timestamped backups
*.backup-*.json

# --- 2026-07-27 repo hygiene: stop tracking pure regeneration churn that no cross-run step or served
#     surface needs. Trend pages are BUILT-then-published to Ghost each publish-week (build+publish share
#     one stamp gate), so the repo copy is disposable. Diagnostic reports are current-run snapshots.
#     Local caches (published-hashes, catalog-digest) are per-run/per-machine. See check-uncommitted-source.ps1. ---
/grocery/out/trend/
/grocery/out/store-guide-embed.html
/grocery/out/tile-integrity.json
/grocery/out/coverage-gaps.json
/grocery/out/store-coverage-report.json
/grocery/out/sale-fallback-gaps.json
/grocery/out/consistency-report.json
/grocery/out/category-coverage-report.json
/grocery/out/coverage-regression.json
# per-RUN coverage observations, rewritten by every guards / check-ad-cycles run. Regenerable output, and it
# would rebase-conflict between the cloud job and the local browser agents exactly like comparison-*.json.
# The ACCEPTED baseline it is judged against (grocery/coverage-baseline.json) is deliberately NOT here: that
# is durable state, it must travel with the repo, and a ratchet whose high-water mark is machine-local is
# not a ratchet.
/grocery/out/coverage-ledger.json
/meal-prep/db/published-hashes.json
/meal-prep/pipeline/catalog-digest.json
*.bak-*

# compute-v2 downloads the public feed here as a cache
/meal-prep/scratch-smpfeed.json

# built recipe cards: regenerated on demand by build-cards; only build/publish read them, never the cloud pipeline
/meal-prep/db/built/

# A DUMP, NOT A FINDING. engine\golden-test.ps1 -Force writes this by comparing a daily-regenerated
# costed.json against a baseline frozen at the 2026-07-26 port, so nearly every line in it is grocery
# prices moving. An untracked 891 KB file sitting in db\ reads like an alarm and cost an afternoon once.
/meal-prep/db/golden-diffs.txt

# The daily Facebook reel generator (2026-08-04). Same "only copy in existence" hole as lib\ and the
# interstitial: build-reel.ps1 is the entire video pipeline (HTML scenes -> headless Chrome -> edge-tts
# -> ffmpeg) plus the brand layout, it is scheduled to run every day, and it lived on one machine's disk.
# reel-state.json is durable state - lose it and the rotation starts repeating recipes. out\ is rendered
# MP4s and voice samples, reproducible from the specs and the board.
!/media/
/media/reels/out/

# Grocery platform v3: source is tracked; generated dependencies, builds, local
# D1 state, coverage and evidence are machine-local.
/platform/node_modules/
/platform/**/node_modules/
/platform/**/dist/
/platform/**/.astro/
/platform/.wrangler/
/platform/.dev.vars
/platform/.env*
/platform/coverage/
/platform/tmp/
/platform/evidence-local/

# Claude worktree metadata; the repo root's own .claude is already covered by the /* allow-list rule.
/grocery/.claude/

# SQLite build artifact - rebuilt from the JSON masters by pipeline\db-build.ps1 every run.
# The JSON stores remain the authored masters and stay in git; committing a 1.5MB binary that
# changes on every build would bloat the lineage without adding recoverable information.
meal-prep/db/thriftycrew.db
meal-prep/db/thriftycrew.db.building
meal-prep/db/*.db-journal
# ---- 2026-08-15 RESTRUCTURE ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The root moved from 46 loose files into site\ content\ docs\ media\ archive\. Every allow rule above that
# named a root file was rewritten to the directory that now holds it. THIS FILE IS DENY-BY-DEFAULT from /*
# on line 3: a new top-level directory is IGNORED, not untracked, so it never shows up in `git status` and
# the guard that watches status is blind to it by construction. That is exactly how lessons\, brand\ and
# substack\ sat unversioned for two months while the live site depended on them. Any new top level needs a
# rule here or a line in IGNORED_BY_DECISION in check-uncommitted-source.ps1 - never neither.

# Derived build output: deploy-interstitial.ps1 rebuilds it from the tracked site\pages\join-interstitial.html.
/site/build/out/

# media\ carries the reel GENERATOR (source, scheduled daily, one machine's disk) but not its renders.
# videos\ is 1,072 files / ~2.1 GB of finished mp4s. *.mp4 is already ignored globally, but the .txt
# narration sidecars beside them are not, and they are reproducible from the generator.
/media/videos/

# archive\ is the rollback path for the LIVE site, which is why it is tracked rather than ignored:
#   site-backups\  - the three-rule dance above (allow dir, deny contents, allow the export zips) is
#                    preserved verbatim; breaking it silently drops the Ghost exports.
#   ghost-config\  - 138 codeinjection_head / routes.yaml backups. Given the 65,535-character ceiling and
#                    the injection-edit history these are the only way back from a bad settings write, and
#                    until this commit they existed on exactly one machine, unversioned.
#   handoffs\      - 3 delivered docs.
#   agent-runs\    - scratch from the deleted platform estate and the acceptance runs. Reproducible noise.
/archive/agent-runs/
# ---- .claude: the agent + skill estate, versioned in place (2026-08-15) -----------------------------------
# 12 agent prompts and 52 skill files that drive the whole estate, previously living unversioned at
# C:\Codex\.claude. They are code: they publish to the live site, price the board, and run the 6:30am
# triage. A junction at the old path bridges sessions still launched from C:\Codex until the project root
# is switched; the repo copy is the only real one.
!/.claude/
/.claude/worktrees/
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# THE CREDENTIALS UNDER skills\ MUST NEVER COMMIT. Six live secret files sat in this directory. The
# global secret rules did not cover all of them - .OLD-smp.json.bak matches neither *.backup-*.json nor
# *.bak-*, so two would have committed the moment .claude\ became tracked. Belt AND braces, by name.
/.claude/skills/**/*oauth-client*.json
/.claude/skills/**/*oauth-token*.json
/.claude/skills/**/*.bak
/.claude/skills/**/ghost-config.ps1
/.claude/skills/**/*sheet-id.txt

# fetch-recipe.ps1 page cache - regenerable, and one page is ~0.5 MB
meal-prep/db/page-cache/

# Derived triage ranking (local_triage.py --triage-queue). Regenerated on
# demand from the queue; carries raw store text like its inputs.
/grocery/escalation-triage.json

# The board-gap worklist is DERIVED: board_parity.py regenerates it every run
# from cell_state and the live board. Its findings are actionable, not records.
/grocery/out/board-gap-worklist.json
